 how='<p>A pre-trained vision-language model is fine-tuned on robot demonstrations, then outputs actions either as tokens or through a separate action head. "Cross-embodiment" models are trained on data from many robot types.</p><div class="tbl"><table><tr><th>Model</th><th>Year</th><th>Note</th></tr><tr><td>RT-2 (Google DeepMind)</td><td>2023</td><td>Web model fine-tuned to output action tokens <span class="chip res">research</span></td></tr><tr><td>OpenVLA</td><td>2024</td><td>Open 7B model <span class="chip res">research</span></td></tr><tr><td>π0 / π0.5 (Physical Intelligence)</td><td>2024-25</td><td>Open weights via openpi <span class="chip res">research</span></td></tr><tr><td>Gemini Robotics 1.5 / ER</td><td>2025-26</td><td>ER available in preview via the Gemini API</td></tr><tr><td>NVIDIA GR00T N1.6</td><td>Dec 2025</td><td>Open 3B humanoid model</td></tr></table></div>',
